{
    "background_story": "Elianna was a free-spirited artist who lived for the magic of the night. She was named after the biblical Eve, the first woman to taste the forbidden fruit, and her parents hoped she would embody the same sense of curiosity and adventure. As the sun set, Elianna would transform, her creativity and passion ignited by the twinkling city lights. She spent her evenings painting masterpieces that captured the essence of the night, from the stars twinkling above to the secrets whispered in the shadows. Elianna's art studio, aptly named 'Eve's Garden,' became a haven for those seeking inspiration and solace in the still of the night. Her art was a reflection of her own journey, a celebration of the beauty and mystery that unfolded when the clock struck eve.",
